course: dictionary
lesson: 3177
title: Empty: nothing inside, or nobody there
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word empty tells you what is missing. Look at the words around it to find out what is gone. «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» Empty space has nothing in it, so there is nothing for sound to travel through.
explain: Empty can also mean with no people. «Shout hello in a big empty hall and a moment later the walls shout it back.» The hall has no people in it, so the only voice you hear is your own, coming back as an echo.
explain: Empty can be a doing word too. To empty is to take everything out. «Empty your bag» means tip out all the things inside it. Try your meaning in the sentence: if you can take everything out, it makes sense.
fact: Empty is an adjective (empty, emptier, emptiest) and a verb (empties, emptied, emptying).
fact: «Empty» as an adjective means with nothing in or on it, as in «an empty box».
fact: «Empty» can also mean with no people, as in «an empty street» or «an empty house».
fact: «On an empty stomach» means without eating any food first.
fact: In science, an empty jar is really full of air, because air fills the space where nothing else is.
exercise: Shout hello in a big empty hall and the walls shout it back. What does empty mean here? | Full of loud music | With nothing on the floor, so you can see the tiles | Covered in paint | *With no people in it
exercise: A tummy rumble is louder when the stomach is empty. What does empty mean here? | It is full of food and drink | It is making a loud noise on purpose | It has just been washed with soap | *It has no food in it
exercise: Saffie gets home to an empty house till six. What does empty mean here? | Very dark and tidy | *No one is at home | Painted white inside | Full of toys and games
test: Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space. Why can't sound travel through empty space? | Because the sound is too small to move | Because sound only travels at night | *Because there is nothing in it for the sound to travel through | Because space is too loud
test: Mum says, «Please empty your bag before bed.» What does empty mean here? | *Take everything out of | Put more things into | Carry it to school | Lock the zip on
exam: Mrs Hughes pops round to check on Saffie in her empty house. What does empty mean here? | *With no people in it | Full of noise and laughter | With nothing in it | To take everything out
